{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7977","id":5219159776,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNxYO4A","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7977","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7977.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7977.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7977","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7977/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7977/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7977/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/d1aa773e0d4eea770a6166975b5655810bba446f","number":7977,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"design(id): server-side invariants — budgets, observability, exploit resistance, containment","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #5962\n\nDesign record for the #5955 worlds program child #5962 (statements S24–S27 of the 2026-11-04 brief). Docs only; no runtime limits, capability defaults, or policy values change.\n\n## What it settles\n\n- **Budget set B1–B7** (§3), each with scope, accounting window, and one primary enforcement class out of **hard refusal / hard termination / throttle / bill**: per-call gas (B1), per-function per-tick fuel (B2), per-world per-tick aggregate (B3), per-session cumulative use (B4), per-world aggregate logical memory (B5), disk/storage per world (B6), library/module cache (B7). Landed numbers cite their constant and file; unsettled numbers are marked TBD with the owning research (#5966 mechanism, #6001 burst/tick calibration, #6002 timeout, #5965 compile/cache economics) and upstream anchors (wasmtime fuel/StoreLimits, Linux rlimits) instead of invented values.\n- **Trip observability** (§4): one trip record (budget, class, stable reason code, scope, accounting, retry), and three audience projections per budget — world author, server admin, and the affected function user — with the fault attribution rule that world-budget exhaustion is explicitly *not* the user's fault (no strike).\n- **Attack-surface checklist** (§5): the guest execution surface (import-free link, export allowlist, fuel/memory/message discipline, poison containment, snapshot fidelity, native rlimits) and a row for **all 20 registered providers** with the concrete bound each one already has, plus the file/network opt-in tier kept **off by default and first-party-only** pending the capability-control testing gate.\n- **Containment** (§6): why per-instance fuel/memory domains, atomic local refusals, and restore-time enforcement keep one world's exhaustion from degrading co-resident worlds; three shared-fate assumptions (A1–A3) and four open questions (O1–O4) stated explicitly.\n- **Reconciliation** (§2, E1–E12): the landed sandbox/world bounds checked against `pkgs/id/src/sandbox.rs`, `pkgs/id/crates/id-core/src/world_limits.rs`, `pkgs/id/src/world/core.rs`, `pkgs/id/crates/id-core/src/world_caps.rs`, `pkgs/id/src/world/mod.rs`, `world_native.rs`, `world_compile.rs`.\n\n## Scope discipline\n\nConsumes #7625's per-user mapping, failure table, and fuel-style fairness without re-deciding any of it; treats the #557 logical-memory ledger as a partial baseline (restore seam only, not disk or full runtime allocation); defers registry/prompt and capability-fact design to #5958/#6017 and compile-cache cost assumptions to #5965.\n\nIndexed in `doc/README.md` and `planning/architecture/README.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\nDoc-only. Every named limit was cross-checked against the cited source file; provider count and default-ceiling membership were generated from `CATALOG_ENTRIES` (20 providers: 14 host + 6 platform modules; 2 excluded-by-default sensor caps). Upstream links fetch 200. No tests run: no code changed.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796793795&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7977&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7977&signature=4c1693fe53a6195a518ab1c3fbcc0b6b46b326ae6b11e61164bcc74779820005\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7977?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T05:23:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T05:32:38Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T05:32:36Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T05:32:36Z","merge_commit_sha":"0405be46651f4b1df915504386245e88560d22f0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/14156-5962-server-invariants","ref":"queue/14156-5962-server-invariants","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":"","language":"Rust","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"watchers":1,"open_issues_count":1276,"open_issues":1276,"size":222650,"default_branch":"main","has_issues"